KG42.register("source_edge_archive-17486cf56006cdc2bb090789",{"id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","paper":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g02-ev33"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-62155e4e7998a74f","target":"COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","source_occurrence_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","target_occurrence_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","source_unit_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-a-M01::bidding.demand","target_unit_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. | SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. | SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. | Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g01-ev-004","v141-b-g01-ev-011","v141-b-g01-ev-014","v141-b-g02-ev33"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"5ebb9c85ee853649283c81e1f9341c018d96fef804a158a75f77998e1a8672c8","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The requested quantity specifies the minimum required active-energy variation relative to the forecasted baseline. Positive quantities denote upward regulation and negative quantities denote downward regulation; the per-period request is expressed in kW h/period. Scope: DSO upward and downward regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market, for each requested period.","target_definition":"The SESP, acting as aggregator, receives DSO flexibility requests specifying minimum active-energy variations relative to the forecast baseline, without knowing grid-status information. Scope: DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. The SESP's coordination of corrective actions must give DSO needs maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads. Scope: SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. Condition: During a DSO-designated yellow-light grid situation. The SESP may send direct control signals overriding local household energy-management decisions. Scope: SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. Condition: During a grid-constrained yellow-light situation. The SESP's forecast must have DSO approval before it is used as the baseline scenario. Scope: Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline. Condition: When a consumption or generation forecast for a flexible asset is to be used as the baseline scenario.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP, acting as aggregator, receives DSO flexibility requests specifying minimum active-energy variations relative to the forecast baseline, without knowing grid-status information. Scope: DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g02-ev33"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-001","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"be In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for or sending information, t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A local flexibility market (LFM) is an electricity trading platform to sell and buy flexibility in geographically limited areas like neighbourhoods and small towns. The SESP is the local market platform provider and community aggregator (AGR). At the same time, the SESP is a BRP from the regulatory point of view because it bids in wholesale markets. In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for sending information, trading for flexibility, and scheduling actions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-003","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":2,"printed_page":"882","section":"2.1. Centralized local flexibility market approaches","anchor_text":"on same distribution transformer have to be members of the same BRP and diﬀerent BRP could not be in","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast  in  this work, AGR receives DSO requests without knowing grid status information to solve grid congestion problems in the daily basis. In order to attend its demands, AGR controls flexible assets using a market-based methodology."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev33","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p08-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":"888","section":"4.5. DSO request constraints","anchor_text":", nd Tkend,c − (V kend,c − Vkstart,c ) me ρk ,c = ∑ γk ,t · t ∀ k ∈ K SP ,∀ c ∈ C (k ) t = Tkstart,c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Finally, DSO constraints represent the request for fulﬁlling upward and downward regulation. These constraints are deﬁned as the minimum required amount of active energy variation with respect to the forecasted baseline scenario and are denoted as DtDSO. Positives and negative values of DtDSO mean upward and downward regulation re-spectively."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. | SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. | SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. | Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g01-ev-004","v141-b-g01-ev-011","v141-b-g01-ev-014","v141-b-g02-ev33"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g02-ev33"]},"paper_scope_note":"There is direct basis for the DSO request, positive and negative regulation relative to the baseline, and SESP operational responsibility; the requested quantity must not be treated as actual supply quantity, nor cost management as the request reception interface."}});
